# Delete/Remove Confirmation

Any button or action that deletes or removes data must show a confirmation dialog using shadcn `AlertDialog` from `@/components/ui/alert-dialog`.

Do not call delete/remove handlers directly from `onClick`. Do not use `window.confirm`, `confirm()`, or a plain `Dialog` for destructive confirmations.

Install the component if missing:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add alert-dialog
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — no confirmation
<Button variant="destructive" onClick={() => onDelete(id)}>
  <Trash2Icon />
</Button>

// ❌ BAD — browser confirm
const confirmed = window.confirm(`Remove "${title}"?`)
if (confirmed) onRemove(id)

// ✅ GOOD — AlertDialog wraps the trigger
import {
  AlertDialog,
  AlertDialogAction,
  AlertDialogCancel,
  AlertDialogContent,
  AlertDialogDescription,
  AlertDialogFooter,
  AlertDialogHeader,
  AlertDialogTitle,
  AlertDialogTrigger,
} from '@/components/ui/alert-dialog'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

<AlertDialog>
  <AlertDialogTrigger
    render={
      <Button variant="destructive" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Delete topic" />
    }
  />
  <AlertDialogContent>
    <AlertDialogHeader>
      <AlertDialogTitle>Delete topic?</AlertDialogTitle>
      <AlertDialogDescription>
        This will permanently delete "{topic.name}". This action cannot be undone.
      </AlertDialogDescription>
    </AlertDialogHeader>
    <AlertDialogFooter>
      <AlertDialogCancel>Cancel</AlertDialogCancel>
      <AlertDialogAction variant="destructive" onClick={() => onDelete(topic.id)}>
        Delete
      </AlertDialogAction>
    </AlertDialogFooter>
  </AlertDialogContent>
</AlertDialog>
```

- Applies to all destructive actions: delete, remove, trash, clear, etc.
- Use `variant="destructive"` on the trigger button and confirm action.
- Describe what will be removed in `AlertDialogDescription`.
- For reusable patterns, extract a small wrapper (e.g. `ConfirmDeleteDialog`) that composes `AlertDialog` primitives.
